  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1229 PM MDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nUpper low is centered near the Four Corners region with upper level\nascent overspreading the region. Precipitation will increase across\nnortheastern WY later this afternoon, spreading into southwestern\nSD into south-central SD after 06z tonight. Precipitation will be\nfocused along the NE/SD border where 0.5-1.25\" of rain is possible\n(probability >0.5\" ~70-80%). Precipitation amounts taper off \nrapidly closer to I-90 with spotty, light amounts north of I-90. \nRain ends Thursday morning as the system pushes east.\n\nUpper level trough pushes through the Northern Plains/Upper Midwest \nlate Wednesday into Thursday. Surface low pressure drops out of\nCanada into the Upper Midwest with a cold front to sweep through \nthe forecast area Thursday morning and afternoon. Gusty northwesterly\nwinds expected behind the front with widespread 40 to 55 mph \ngusts, strongest across northwestern SD and portions of the \nwestern SD plains. A Wind Advisory is now in effect for these \nareas. Transient high wind gusts (> 60 mph) are possible, although\ncoverage and frequency do not warrant High Wind headlines.\n\nCold air advection and clearing skies will result in widespread \nfreezing/sub-freezing temperatures Thursday night into Friday \nmorning for the majority of the forecast area.\n\nUpper level ridging quickly builds over the western half of the \ncountry Friday into the weekend. Above average temperatures are \nforecast for the weekend into early next week with elevated fire \nweather conditions.",
